SPLogbook for Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (Debian binary package)
======================================================

Supported system
----------------

This package targets 64-bit systems that provide glibc 2.43 (GLIBC_2.43)
or newer. The reference and only tested distribution is Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.
Debian 13.7 (glibc 2.41) and openSUSE Leap 16.1 (glibc 2.40) do not satisfy
the binary ABI requirement and are not supported. RPM-based and Arch-based
distributions must use their own package formats.

Installation layout
-------------------

  /opt/SPLogbook/SPLogbook                     main executable
  /opt/SPLogbook/splogbook-updater             updater helper
  /opt/SPLogbook/lib/libhamlib.so.4            bundled Hamlib library
  /opt/SPLogbook/locales/                      user interface translations
  /opt/SPLogbook/LICENSE                       GPL-3.0-or-later license text
  /opt/SPLogbook/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/         third-party license texts
  /opt/SPLogbook/.splogbook-deb-marker         package identity marker
  /usr/bin/splogbook                           minimal launcher
  /usr/share/applications/splogbook.desktop    desktop entry
  /usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/splogbook.png
  /usr/share/doc/splogbook/README.Debian       this file
  /usr/share/doc/splogbook/copyright           copyright and license

User data
---------

The package never stores user data in /opt/SPLogbook. SPLogbook keeps its
data in the XDG base directories:

  $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/splogbook    configuration (fallback ~/.config/splogbook)
  $XDG_DATA_HOME/splogbook      QSO databases (fallback ~/.local/share/splogbook)
  $XDG_STATE_HOME/splogbook     state and logs (fallback ~/.local/state/splogbook)
  $XDG_CACHE_HOME/splogbook     cache (fallback ~/.cache/splogbook)

Installation, upgrade, removal and purge of this package do not modify or
delete QSO databases, WAL/SHM files, station configuration, ADIF/Cabrillo
exports, backups or device configuration in the user's home directory.

Updates
-------

This package is system-managed. SPLogbook detects the DEB installation and
delegates updates to the system package manager; it never runs sudo, pkexec
or doas and never replaces files in /usr or /opt by itself. Update the
package with the distribution package manager, for example:

  sudo apt update
  sudo apt install --only-upgrade splogbook

Serial port access
------------------

Access to serial/USB CAT interfaces may require the operator account to be
a member of the dialout group. The package does not change user accounts or
group membership; the local administrator decides that separately.

-- SPLogbook packaging, M3-H
